{
  "correction_rules": [
    "Persistent low bias: model systematically underestimates the realized uptrend. Apply an upward level shift that increases with horizon (small in days 1–5, larger from ~day 10 onward).",
    "Trend/acceleration lag: when the last 1–2 weeks show a rising regime (higher highs), the forecast responds too slowly. Add a momentum term based on the last 5–10 day slope to lift the whole path.",
    "Horizon-specific underpricing: errors are modest early but grow materially mid-to-late horizon (≈days 10–30). Use a horizon-weighted correction (e.g., linear ramp) rather than a flat adjustment.",
    "Peaks too low / rallies capped: during strong rallies the model produces local maxima ~2–4 EUR below realized. Increase forecast volatility/upside by scaling positive moves (asymmetric adjustment: boost positive deviations more than negative).",
    "Mean-reversion too strong: after dips, the model reverts to the prior mean, but the market continues trending higher. Reduce mean-reversion strength when recent realized volatility + positive drift are elevated."
  ]
}
